{
    "background_story": "In a lush, prehistoric forest, Princess roamed as a majestic Stegosaurus, a member of the Thyreophora clade. Her row of plates running down her back glistened in the sunlight, a defense mechanism that warned potential predators to stay away. Despite her intimidating appearance, Princess was a gentle giant, feeding on ferns and cycads. She was a devoted mother, carefully guarding her nest and teaching her young ones how to use their spiked tails for defense. As she wandered through the forest, Princess left behind a trail of crushed plants, creating pathways for other herbivores to follow. Her name 'Princess' was a nod to her regal demeanor and the crown-like plates on her head, which shone like a royal diadem.",
